Powers and Functions of the TCCP. The TCCP shall perform the following powers and
Provide overall policy direction for the Philippine Technical Cooperation Program;
Approve the Philippine Technical Cooperation Roadmap and Program;
Ensure alignment of technical cooperation initiatives with national development priorities and foreign policy
objectives;
Facilitate inter-agency coordination and stakeholder engagement; and
Perform such other functions as may be necessary or incidental to the mandate of the TCCP.

TCCP Secretariat. The TCCP Secretariat shall be fully integrated to the DFA, and shall provide
technical, administrative, and coordination support to the TCCP.
The TCCP Secretariat shall perform the following functions:
Prepare technical reports, policy briefs, and recommendations for consideration by the TCCP;
Coordinate with implementing agencies and development partners in the preparation of project documents and
agreements;
Monitor and evaluate the implementation of technical cooperation programs and projects;
Maintain a database of ongoing and completed technical cooperation initiatives;
Provide secretariat services, including preparation of meeting agendas, minutes, and related documentation;
Coordinate inter-agency inputs to ensure coherent representation of Philippine technical cooperation interests
at the bilateral, regional, and multilateral levels; and
Submit regular reports to the TCCP.
The TCCP Secretariat shall be under control and supervision of the Office of the Secretary of Foreign Affairs,
and supervision may be assigned to a senior official who may serve as Chair-Alternate.
